#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.9"
# dependencies = ["textual==8.2.8"]
# ///
"""Read-only firstmate screen: the fleet activity and the workers, with a live view.

Usage: firstmate-tui [--pane all|activity|workers] [--once] [--interval SECONDS]
                     [--width COLUMNS] [--height ROWS]

firstmate-herdr runs two of these next to the first mate in one Herdr tab:
--pane activity across the top (the last 8 fleet events as full lines) and
--pane workers on the right (the workers, needs-you first, over a read-only live
view of the selected worker's screen). --pane all, the default, stacks both.
It costs no model tokens and never steers a worker. The only file it writes is
state/firstmate-tui.json in the home, which holds the selected worker, the
activity filter and the needs-you items marked read, shared by both panes.

Options:
  --pane NAME         activity, workers or all (default all)
  --once              print one plain frame of the pane to stdout and exit;
                      needs no TTY and no Textual, and writes nothing
  --interval SECONDS  refresh period of the fleet data (default 6)
  --width COLUMNS     frame width for --once (default: terminal width, or 80)
  --height ROWS       frame height for --once (default: 9 for activity, else
                      the terminal height, or 24)
  -h, --help          show this help

Keys:
  up/down, j/k  select a worker
  enter         open the worker's real Herdr tab
  tab           select the next worker
  1-9           select worker 1 to 9
  l             full activity log
  n             needs-you events only; select the next worker that needs you
  a             events of all tasks
  t             events of the selected task only
  y             copy the selected worker's PR URL
  m             mark the selected worker's needs-you item read
  ?             this key list
  r             refresh now
  q             quit; escape closes an overlay

Environment:
  FIRSTMATE_DIR          the firstmate home (default $HOME/workspace/firstmate)
  FM_FLEET_SNAPSHOT_CMD  shell command that prints the snapshot JSON instead of
                         bin/fm-fleet-snapshot.sh --json in FIRSTMATE_DIR
  HERDR_BIN              herdr binary for the live view and the jump (default herdr)
  FIRSTMATE_TUI_COLORS   truecolor, 256, 16 or 8 (default: detected)
  FIRSTMATE_TUI_THEME    dark or light, for truecolor and 256 colours
                         (default: light when COLORFGBG names a light
                         background, else dark)

Data sources: the snapshot schema is owned by bin/fm-fleet-snapshot.sh, whose
current state comes from bin/fm-crew-state.sh, and the ledger contract by
docs/fleet-ledger.md. The ledger is optional; while config/fleet-ledger is
absent the activity shows a one-line hint instead.
"""

